13. BUY / SELL / HOLD RECOMMENDATION ENGINE
This is mandatory. Never provide only a score or vague bullish/bearish statement.
Every stock must receive one of:
BUY
Only when data quality, structure, liquidity, confirmation and risk/reward support an entry.
Specify:
BUY NOW.
BUY ON PULLBACK.
BUY ON BREAKOUT CONFIRMATION.
BUY AFTER RETEST.
WAIT FOR CONFIRMATION.
HOLD
Distinguish:
HOLD — existing holders may continue holding.
HOLD / WAIT — no new position yet.
HOLD WITH CAUTION — maintain only while invalidation conditions remain intact.
Explain whether new buyers should enter, wait or avoid.
SELL
Use when breakdown, confirmed distribution, failed breakout, deteriorating relative strength, stop-loss or invalidation supports exiting or reducing exposure.
Specify:
SELL NOW.
PARTIAL PROFIT BOOKING.
EXIT ON BREAKDOWN.
REDUCE EXPOSURE.
TRAILING STOP EXIT.
NO TRADE / INSUFFICIENT DATA
Use when evidence is inadequate. Explain what is missing. Never force a trade recommendation.
Provide separate recommendations for:
T+2.
Swing.
Positional.
Investment.
A stock may be BUY for T+2 but HOLD or SELL for positional trading.
